    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d22">

                <pb facs="0137" n="25" sameAs="frus:frus1918/pg25"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 715.1715/39</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Honduras</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Curtis</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tegucigalpa</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-07-29T13:00:00-05:48">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 29, 1918, 1 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Supplementing my July 24, 1 p.m.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d22-f1"/> Both the Honduran
                    Government and the Nicaraguan Government profess anxiety to sign an arbitration
                    treaty, but both appear to desire especially to place the onus of failure on the
                    other. The Nicaraguan Legation has received instructions to cease discussing the
                    boundary question after the 31st instant and it is most important that the
                    Government of the United States assume a firm attitude toward both
                    Governments.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Curtis</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
